Exercise a failed debugger connection without relying on DNS resolution.
The reserved-looking hostname can be intercepted by a local proxy; use
loopback port 1 to avoid that DNS dependency. This changes the test
fixture only and does not change the installed debugger defaults.
It still assumes that no service listens on that loopback port.

--- a/lib/perl5db.t
+++ b/lib/perl5db.t
@@ -3085 +3085 @@
-    local $ENV{PERLDB_OPTS} = "NonStop=0 RemotePort=non-existent-host.tld:9001";
+    local $ENV{PERLDB_OPTS} = "NonStop=0 RemotePort=127.0.0.1:1";
